      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $f$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $-4.5$ | $-3$ | $-2.5$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $29.25$ | $15$ | $11.25$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $5.25$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $f(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{29.25,15,11.25,3,0,-1,5.25\\}.$",
